<script setup lang="ts">
// Vendor marks for the deploy pick page, in their real brand colors.
//  - Qwen: the 2026 rebrand mark, inlined from the official asset, Qwen blue.
//  - OpenAI: the official Blossom (from OpenAI's own brand SVGs), drawn in
//    currentColor - that renders it black on light and white on dark, which
//    is exactly the two official variants.
//  - Google: the 2025 gradient "G" as an <img> asset, because its SVG carries
//    gradient/filter defs whose ids must stay scoped to the file, not leak
//    into the page.
//  - Poolside: the official wave mark (from poolside.ai), inlined in
//    currentColor like OpenAI. Its defs (fade gradient on the ring, the
//    circle mask, clip) carry ids, and this component renders many times on
//    one page - useId() scopes them per instance so references never cross
//    logos. The source SVG's `mask=s1` id typo is fixed to `mask-s1` here.
//  - IBM: the 8-bar logo, in currentColor like OpenAI (black on light, white
//    on dark are both official marks). Two things differ from every other
//    entry here. It is a WORDMARK with no square icon variant, so it is fit
//    to HEIGHT and the width follows the 58:23 ratio - letterboxed into a
//    size×size box it would be 5.5px tall at the inline call sites, where its
//    eight bars fall under a pixel each and alias into a smear. And IBM's
//    markup colors the mark from CSS, so its wrapper group carries
//    fill="none"; kept as-is that renders nothing, so the fill moved onto the
//    path (fill-rule="evenodd" came off the same group).
//  - KBLab (kb-whisper): the National Library of Sweden lab's full-color
//    mark as an <img> asset - same reasoning as Google, its gradient defs
//    keep their ids scoped to the file.
//  - NB AI-Lab (nb-whisper): the National Library of Norway mark in its
//    brand red, with a dark-theme lift like Qwen.
//  - CoRal Project: the Alexandra Institute's mark (the project's maker),
//    monochrome, so currentColor like OpenAI/IBM.
//  - Prism ML: the official header emblem, with the wordmark cropped off;
//    path geometry preserved, currentColor for both themes. Source:
//    https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/697a3312d33c2cc715ec3899/69961847735f3ec32aafc18e_prism-logo.svg
//  - Aleph Alpha (Kolibri): the official emblem from aleph-alpha.com's header,
//    the wordmark beside it left off. Monochrome in the source (#171717), so
//    currentColor like OpenAI/IBM; path geometry and viewBox unchanged. Source:
//    https://aleph-alpha.com/_astro/logo-bm.C1UmWdTa_ZKMPHl.svg
//  - Everyone else (the cloud-model makers): official marks from
//    simple-icons, drawn in currentColor so they read in both themes -
//    same treatment as OpenAI/IBM. Brands simple-icons doesn't carry
//    (xAI, Tencent, Z.ai, Cohere...) fall to the letter badge below.
// Keyed by the catalog's `vendor` field (the maker, not the brand title).
